<!--
    decbench cases-missing pool: coreutils 'comm' main (x86-64, GCC -O0, PIE,
    stripped), entry 0x3994 in the original image.  The mapped code runs past
    main's end and the second chunk is its .rodata jump table; both only bound
    main's flow, exactly as read symbols does for the whole ELF.

    Stage model: S2 lift/flow, switch-model sub-stage.  P0 assertion:
    `option loweredswitch on|off` (DIV-4, default-on).

    The bug.  main's getopt_long dispatch has TWO switch shapes: a comparison
    cascade over the small option characters ('1'/'2'/'3' and the negative
    help/version sentinels) AND a genuine GCC PIC relative-offset jump table at
    0x3aed (`notrack jmp rax`, table at 0x9800) for the dense 0x7a..0x83 range.
    `loweredswitch` fires on the cascade and rewires its head to a synthetic
    BRANCHIND, which strands the real table's block; the trailing
    `removeUnreachableBlocks` sweep then destroyed that block's ops WITHOUT
    dropping its JumpTable (the ported `blockRemoveInternal` had the
    `findJumpTable`/`removeJumpTable` arm stubbed out).  `ActionSwitchNorm` later
    re-recovered the model of that stale table and walked the destroyed
    BRANCHIND's nulled inputs, panicking in `findDeterminingVarnodes`, so the whole
    function decompiled to nothing.  (Same failure on join and uniq main, at -O0
    and -O2.)

    The fix (no option, a strict bug fix on both counts):
      * `blockRemoveInternal` now drops a removed BRANCHIND's jump table, and
        `ActionSwitchNorm` skips a table whose indirect op is gone;
      * `kunaInstallLoweredSwitch` DECLINES when its rewiring would strand a
        block whose tail BRANCHIND already owns a recovered JumpTable, so the
        genuine switch is kept instead of being replaced by the cascade dispatch.

    Pass 1 runs the DEFAULT pipeline (`loweredswitch on`): before the fix it
    panicked and emitted no body, so every count below was zero or half.
    Pass 2 (`option loweredswitch off`) is the reference rendering: the real
    jump-table switch over 0x7a/0x80..0x83 with the cascade left as if/else.
    The two passes must now agree, because the install declines.
-->
